    "body": "No; a [valid time-zone offset string](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-microsyntaxes.html#valid-time-zone-offset-string) is the only thing allowed. You can see examples of that above the text you quote.\r\n\r\nThis note is just explaining that timezone offsets aren't as useful, and you might want to instead say something like `2020-01-09T00:00 in New York`.\r\n\r\nPerhaps we could add an example showing that.",
